<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12152"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 24, 2005 - 5:55 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Larry Christopher Graham, a former boyfriend of Susan Bugay was found guilty of her daughter&#39;s murder in August 2002. Graham abducted Angela Bugay on November 19 1983 while she accompanied her younger brother to retrieve his boots from their apartment in Antioch. Angela Bugay&#39;s corpse was discovered a week later in a shallow grave in a secluded field a short distance from the apartment. Graham was arrested in 1996 after forensic scientists matched his DNA to the seminal fluid obtained from the corpse. In October 2002, Graham was sentenced to death. <BR> <BR>John Philpin&#39;s book contains a photograph of Angela Bugay&#39;s grave at the Oakmont cemetery.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
