<!--Post: 12470--><!--Time: 1112272132-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12470"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tallulabay<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tallulabay<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 31, 2005 - 4:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To add to that if above and not below, then invasive species, that is those seeds not from normal top soil activity of graves will show a different density and pattern especially now, so if you are walking around the perimeter look at where a colony is now coming up in the next few weeks. If however, someone with the knowledge obtained by being or associatiing with a grave digger had used this nocturnal hiding place as a holding centre then the police obviously have to get this surveyed with the help of forensic archeologists and anthropologists.  <BR> <BR>I believe that the material and comments from those involved and reading the book which I have not read and my psychic intuition relayed to the correct authorities will expose the pattern of behaviours of those involved. There has been sadi the girls are alive and been abducted, but this has not been the case with the majority of victims so far found. The skull, now that is old Norse stuff, and one that as a tactic is as old as the Hills as Anderson knows. By confusing when a victim died, and where the rest of the remains may be it sets the Bindner glorification of his self importance in being a star witness behind. Anderson then takes full credit as alternative locations, and explanations. Me, with the experts involved we will with LE find the children, geology is my main field, so watch out for what I am seeing and lookin for. Spring is coming. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
